[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392732135","pull_request_review_id":3286579692,"id":2392732135,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6OnjHn","diff_hunk":"@@ -623,6 +610,13 @@ bool ClassDB::_can_instantiate(ClassInfo *p_class_info, bool p_exposed_only) {\n \t\treturn false;\n \t}\n \n+#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED\n+\t// Force legacy unexposed classes to skip the exposed check to preserve backcompat.\n+\tif (p_class_info->gdextension && p_class_info->gdextension->legacy_unexposed_class) {\n+\t\tp_exposed_only = false;","path":"core/object/class_db.cpp","commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","original_commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Hrm... if the class was registered to be unexposed, we need to prevent `class_get_default_property_value` from instantiating it, right?\nWon't this check _allow_ them to instantiate it? I get that we need to allow e.g. the editor to instantiate it, because that's what we made the fix for, but I think otherwise https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108614#issuecomment-3335505455 may not be fixed with this.","created_at":"2025-09-30T20:16:08Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T20:17:08Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392732135","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392732135"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392732135"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392732135/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":616,"original_line":616,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":82,"position":82,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392741180","pull_request_review_id":3286592774,"id":2392741180,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6OnlU8","diff_hunk":"@@ -623,6 +610,13 @@ bool ClassDB::_can_instantiate(ClassInfo *p_class_info, bool p_exposed_only) {\n \t\treturn false;\n \t}\n \n+#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED\n+\t// Force legacy unexposed classes to skip the exposed check to preserve backcompat.\n+\tif (p_class_info->gdextension && p_class_info->gdextension->legacy_unexposed_class) {\n+\t\tp_exposed_only = false;","path":"core/object/class_db.cpp","commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","original_commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I didn't do exactly what we discussed at the meeting. Instead, I rolled back the changes from PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108614 so it's no longer forcing old unexposed classes to be exposed: they are now actually registered as unexposed.\r\n\r\nSo, now the usual protections for unexposed classes will kick in and prevent `class_get_default_property_value()` from instantiating the class.\r\n\r\nWhat this code is doing is making it so that unexposed classes from old (legacy) GDExtensions will allow `ClassDB::instantiate()` to work like it used it. Essentially, trying to solve the same issue as https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108614, but in a different way, which still allows the classes to be marked as unexposed","created_at":"2025-09-30T20:20:19Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T20:21:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392741180","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392741180"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392741180"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392741180/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":616,"original_line":616,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2392732135,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":82,"position":82,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392751776","pull_request_review_id":3286607199,"id":2392751776,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6Onn6g","diff_hunk":"@@ -623,6 +610,13 @@ bool ClassDB::_can_instantiate(ClassInfo *p_class_info, bool p_exposed_only) {\n \t\treturn false;\n \t}\n \n+#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED\n+\t// Force legacy unexposed classes to skip the exposed check to preserve backcompat.\n+\tif (p_class_info->gdextension && p_class_info->gdextension->legacy_unexposed_class) {\n+\t\tp_exposed_only = false;","path":"core/object/class_db.cpp","commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","original_commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I see. The approach sounds like an improvement over what we discussed.\nBut isn't the 'usual protection' preventing `class_get_default_property_value`  from instantiating the class the fact that the class is unexposed (in the below check)?","created_at":"2025-09-30T20:25:17Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T20:25:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392751776","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392751776"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392751776"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392751776/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":616,"original_line":616,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2392732135,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":82,"position":82,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392752566","pull_request_review_id":3286608365,"id":2392752566,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6OnoG2","diff_hunk":"@@ -623,6 +610,13 @@ bool ClassDB::_can_instantiate(ClassInfo *p_class_info, bool p_exposed_only) {\n \t\treturn false;\n \t}\n \n+#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED\n+\t// Force legacy unexposed classes to skip the exposed check to preserve backcompat.\n+\tif (p_class_info->gdextension && p_class_info->gdextension->legacy_unexposed_class) {\n+\t\tp_exposed_only = false;","path":"core/object/class_db.cpp","commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","original_commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Or, actually, maybe I went too far on the `ClassDB::_can_instantiate()` change? Let me do some extra testing...","created_at":"2025-09-30T20:25:36Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T20:25:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392752566","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392752566"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392752566"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392752566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":616,"original_line":616,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2392732135,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":82,"position":82,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392821851","pull_request_review_id":3286699834,"id":2392821851,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6On5Bb","diff_hunk":"@@ -623,6 +610,13 @@ bool ClassDB::_can_instantiate(ClassInfo *p_class_info, bool p_exposed_only) {\n \t\treturn false;\n \t}\n \n+#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED\n+\t// Force legacy unexposed classes to skip the exposed check to preserve backcompat.\n+\tif (p_class_info->gdextension && p_class_info->gdextension->legacy_unexposed_class) {\n+\t\tp_exposed_only = false;","path":"core/object/class_db.cpp","commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","original_commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Alright, I did some more testing, and I think my changes _are_ correct as far as preserving the behavior of Godot 4.4.1 and earlier for old extensions. However, that behavior is a little weird :-)\r\n\r\nUsing godot-cpp on its `4.4` branch, I registered an internal class called `ExampleInternal` with a single integer property, and ran this code:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\tprint(\"ClassDB.class_exists: \", ClassDB.class_exists(\"ExampleInternal\"))\r\n\tprint(\"ClassDB.can_instantiate: \", ClassDB.can_instantiate(\"ExampleInternal\"))\r\n\tprint(\"ClassDB.instantiate: \", ClassDB.instantiate(\"ExampleInternal\"))\r\n\tprint(\"ClassDB.class_get_property_default_value: \", ClassDB.class_get_property_default_value(\"ExampleInternal\", \"value\"))\r\n```\r\n\r\nOn Godot 4.4.1, it's produced this output:\r\n\r\n```\r\nClassDB.class_exists: true\r\nClassDB.can_instantiate: true\r\nClassDB.instantiate: <ExampleInternal#31306286466>\r\nClassDB.class_get_property_default_value: 33\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo, Godot 4.4.1 _doesn't_ prevent `class_get_property_default_value()` from working for internal classes!\r\n\r\nHowever, if I add a `print_line(\"...\")` to the constructor for `ExampleInternal`, when I open the project in the editor with Godot 4.4.1, it _doesn't_ print out that line. Whereas when I open the same project with Godot 4.5, it _does_ print out that line.\r\n\r\nSo, while `class_get_property_default_value()` would work if called, it appears the editor won't call it, if the class is marked as unexposed.\r\n\r\nThis PR should bringing the behavior for unexposed classes from old GDExtensions back in line with Godot 4.4.1, including the results of my GDScript code snippet above, and prevent the [reported crash](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108614#issuecomment-3335505455), but still leaves `class_get_property_default_value()` as potential landmine, just like it was in Godot 4.4.1\r\n\r\nThis exploration just makes me feel more right about the change we made in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102440 :-) - it is much more rational than how Godot 4.4.1 behaves.","created_at":"2025-09-30T20:58:58Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T20:58:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392821851","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392821851"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392821851"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392821851/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":616,"original_line":616,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2392732135,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":82,"position":82,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392831721","pull_request_review_id":3286713532,"id":2392831721,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6On7bp","diff_hunk":"@@ -623,6 +610,13 @@ bool ClassDB::_can_instantiate(ClassInfo *p_class_info, bool p_exposed_only) {\n \t\treturn false;\n \t}\n \n+#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED\n+\t// Force legacy unexposed classes to skip the exposed check to preserve backcompat.\n+\tif (p_class_info->gdextension && p_class_info->gdextension->legacy_unexposed_class) {\n+\t\tp_exposed_only = false;","path":"core/object/class_db.cpp","commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","original_commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Awesome, thanks a lot for testing!\r\nDo you happen to know what line exactly is preventing Godot 4.5 from trying to get the property default value? I think I'm still not following where it's rejecting `_can_instantiate_class`.","created_at":"2025-09-30T21:04:20Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T21:04:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392831721","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392831721"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392831721"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392831721/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":616,"original_line":616,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2392732135,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":82,"position":82,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392879628","pull_request_review_id":3286775089,"id":2392879628,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6OoHIM","diff_hunk":"@@ -623,6 +610,13 @@ bool ClassDB::_can_instantiate(ClassInfo *p_class_info, bool p_exposed_only) {\n \t\treturn false;\n \t}\n \n+#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED\n+\t// Force legacy unexposed classes to skip the exposed check to preserve backcompat.\n+\tif (p_class_info->gdextension && p_class_info->gdextension->legacy_unexposed_class) {\n+\t\tp_exposed_only = false;","path":"core/object/class_db.cpp","commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","original_commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> I think I'm still not following where it's rejecting `_can_instantiate_class`.\r\n\r\nIt's not rejecting it. On Godot 4.4.1, `_can_instantiate_class()` is returning `true` for unexposed classes, and so this PR maintains this behavior for old GDExtensions.\r\n\r\nSo, if `class_get_property_default_values()` were called on an unexposed class from an old GDExtension, it could cause problems, which is why I called it a \"landmine\" above :-)\r\n\r\nIt seems that the editor just doesn't call it on unexposed classes.\r\n\r\nI think it might be this line that's responsible for that:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4a1c1c483beda0997e8e77fe76d43dac4d608d03/editor/doc/doc_tools.cpp#L423\r\n","created_at":"2025-09-30T21:31:53Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T21:31:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392879628","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392879628"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392879628"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392879628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":616,"original_line":616,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2392732135,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":82,"position":82,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392888561","pull_request_review_id":3286787582,"id":2392888561,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6OoJTx","diff_hunk":"@@ -623,6 +610,13 @@ bool ClassDB::_can_instantiate(ClassInfo *p_class_info, bool p_exposed_only) {\n \t\treturn false;\n \t}\n \n+#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED\n+\t// Force legacy unexposed classes to skip the exposed check to preserve backcompat.\n+\tif (p_class_info->gdextension && p_class_info->gdextension->legacy_unexposed_class) {\n+\t\tp_exposed_only = false;","path":"core/object/class_db.cpp","commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","original_commit_id":"2c707a911f09e9c58214c91ae8b5f28146ae098f","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Ohh, right, it's doing its own checks too. That makes sense. Yea, I totally agree that's a landmine. But as long as it doesn't detonate 'by default', that's probably good enough.","created_at":"2025-09-30T21:36:53Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T21:36:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392888561","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392888561"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111090#discussion_r2392888561"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111090"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2392888561/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":616,"original_line":616,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2392732135,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":82,"position":82,"subject_type":"line"}]